Sugriva hails fire-made friendship as highest grace --- Sugriva seats the brothers on sala branches --- Sugriva tells living fearful and wifeless on Rishyamuka --- Sugriva begs protection from world-feared Vali --- Rama laughs and vows to kill the wife-stealer --- Rama shows keen arrows like Indra thunderbolts --- Sugriva weeps and tells deposition and wife seizure --- Sugriva names elder Vali the foe barring his joy --- Rama asks the quarrel cause to weigh strength
